UC018 Recommend for Lease Renewal
Use Case Name	Recommend Lease Renewal  
Use Case Number	UC018
Use Descriptions:	This use case enables the user to identify tenants whose leases are nearing expiry and recommend whether their lease should be renewed. The recommendation is based on predefined business rules and data such as payment history, occupancy duration, tenant behavior, etc.
Primary Actor	Client Services Officer, Tenant
Secondary Actor(s)	Property Lease Management System 
Pre-condition(s)	The lease must be due to lapse in the next three months
User logged in on the system
Trigger	Lease reaches a predefined threshold before expiry (3 months before lease end date)
Success End Condition	Recommendation successfully sent for review 
Failed End Condition	Unable to send recommendation
Screen References	

mSCOA ID	N/A
Integration	IR04 Billing and Revenue Management (Not Ready to be Tested)
	IR06 Credit Control Management (Not Ready to be Tested)
Business Requirements	Requirement ID	Requirement Description
	FR10.1	System generated notification for back-office staff that provides a list of tenants due for lease renewal (3 months before Expiry Date)
	FR10.2	The Official must be able to recommend for renewal
	FR10.4	Tenant must have an option to indicate whether they intend to continue with the lease or terminate
Business Rules	Rule ID 	Rule Description
	BR20	The tenants must be informed of their lease expiry date three (3) months in advance and must be given an opportunity to renew or not
	BR21	Lease renewals must not exceed 72 months period. i.e. lease can only be renewed up to 3 times
	BR39	Tenant must have ≥ 95% on-time payments and there are no active legal disputes
Main Success Scenario [The steps of the scenario from trigger to goal delivery, as well as any clean-up]
Ref	Actor Action	Ref	System Response
Step 1	Select Agreements from the main menu > Click on Lease Agreements > Select Renewals	Step 2	Displays list of applications with status = Flagged for Lease Renewal

Step 3	Select Lease Agreement of interest	Step 4	Accepts user selection
If there is a notification from Tenant to not renew, proceed to Lease Termination process
Step 5	Click Lease Review	Step 6	Displays Evaluating Application Screen with:
+	Tenant and Occupant(s) Details
+	Lease Duration (start & end date)
+	Payment History
+	Rental Arrears or Disputes
+	Complaints Against Tenant
+	Maintenance Issues
+	Tenant Compliance Records (e.g. ITC/TPN checks)
Step 7	View the necessary details and Click Outcome	Step 8	Displays options to select from:
-	Recommended for Renewal
-	Not Recommended for Renewal
-	Review Required
Step 9	Select the appropriate option	Step 10	Accepts user selection and prompts to upload supporting documents
Step 11	Upload supporting documents and Click Submit	Step 12	Displays pop-up confirmation message
Step 13	Click on “Yes, I am sure”	Step 14	Success message displayed and notification sent to Tenant and Revenue Manager
Lease Agreement status = Awaiting Renewal Review Outcome
Alternative Flow: Alternative at Step 13
Step 13	Click Cancel	Step 14	Transaction is cancelled
Main Success Scenario 2: Tenant
Step 1	Select Inbox	Step 2	Displays items in Inbox
Step 3	Select the lease expiry notification	Step 4	Accepts user selection
Step 5	Select Renew Lease option	Step 6	Accepts user selection
Step 7	Click on Submit	Step 8	Displays pop-up confirmation message
Step 9	Click on “Yes, I am sure”	Step 10	Success message displayed and notification sent to Client Services Officer
Alternate Flow 2: Alternative at Step 5
Step 5	Select Do Not Renew Lease option	Step 6	Accepts user selection
Step 7	Click on Submit	Step 8	Displays pop-up confirmation message
Step 9	Click on “Yes, I am sure”	Step 10	Success message displayed and notification sent to Client Services Officer
Client Services Officer initiates Lease Termination process
Note:
The same process should be repeated for the 2nd and 3rd Lease Renewal Recommendation

